Z||000000||AL||12-24-2000||02:50 AM||||<BR>well guys i decide to go to this guys house luckily he was home,i told him who i was and he proceded on showing me the indy.well the car is dirty on the outside but nothing a little water and waxs won't fixs, th engine is pretty clean no oil spots or nothing,the interior is perfect,no tears in corners and the seats where good also.i asked the guy if there were no expired tag penalties on the car, he said he would find out this week,i told him if there were penalties i wouldn't buy it,but if he discounted the penalaties off the price i would,so now i wait to see if there is no penalties and if there is none then i take it home with me.question did indys come with leather seats?cause this one sure did have leather seats,also this car is from arizona i shouldn't have a problem smoging this car,even arizona cars have the smog system in them too,right! i'll keep you posted,<B>AL</B>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AL_sig.gif">  <P>------------------<BR> <p>[This message has been edited by AL (edited 12-24-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||beachbomb||12-24-2000||05:46 PM||||Hey Al! Indy's sure did come with leather seats, light gray leather with red cloth in the middle with the Indy 500 logo embossed into the backrest. How much are the penalties you talk about, must be alot not to buy this Indy! Smog shouldn't be a prob, make sure its got a good Cat. Conv. on it. Other Indys specific items to look for are: Light grey leather steering wheel, light grey leather shift knob(of which i need one if anyone has an extra), light grey leather door pulls, Indy specific air cleaner holder and valve cover gasket(these should be painted light grey with black stripes and 2.5L EFI on the air intake, Indy 500 badges on both fronts fenders and on nose...if you have any question about Indys, plmk, good luck , let us know what happens..Jim(2 '84 Indys) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000002||AL||12-24-2000||06:12 PM||||hey beach in calif if you don't put the car on inop and let the tags expire and don't pay those tags for 6 yrs well that could add up to be big money in penalties,as for the indy,beach it is so clean the interior is clean and the  engine is clean ,if i get this car i will post pics and tell you how lucky i was in finding this jewel.well i will email you if i have any indy questions ok,merry christmas fiero brother<B>AL</B>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AL_sig.gif">  <P>------------------<BR> <p>[This message has been edited by AL (edited 12-24-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Philphine||12-24-2000||06:22 PM||||so... all that "offial pace car" stuff isn't standard on an indy's doors? i don't have them but wasn't sure if it was because of a repaint or something.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||beachbomb||12-24-2000||09:50 PM||||Hi. the "offcial pace car" decals were original equipment. When you bought a new Indy the decals came in the glove box thingy!!, pontiac left it up the the buyer if they wanted the decals on the door or not, the two i own do not have the decals, i wish they did!. From my understanding its harder to find one with the decals then without. You can buy aftermarket decals..later..Jim(2 '84 Indys) ||||reg||10
